---
/* ============================================================
   Bearings — /combinations (drug-combination reference)

   A read-only reference, not a shelf and not a card: no
   motivations, no horizon, no reflection prompt. Someone arrives
   here with a specific question and leaves once it is answered.

   Why it is a page of its own rather than card content: this is
   lookup material, and lookup material that lives inside prose is
   material nobody can find at the moment they need it.

   It is deliberately NOT on the `between` shelf. PRODUCT_BOUNDARY.md
   caps that shelf at zero authored cards, and this page does not
   change that decision — a static reference table rendered the same
   for everyone is a different kind of artifact from advice authored
   for someone mid-experience.

   It states what the data says and stops there. It cannot screen,
   approve, or clear anyone for anything.

   Nothing here touches storage: no selection is persisted, no
   analytics, no network. The dataset ships with the app.
   ============================================================ */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CombinationLookup from "../components/CombinationLookup.svelte";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Combinations — Bearings"
  description="A plain reference for what is known about combining two substances: a status, what that status means, and any note attached to the pairing."
  section="combinations"
>
  <section class="reading">
    <p class="kicker">Reference</p>
    <h1>Combinations</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A plain lookup for two substances at a time: the status the data gives
      that pairing, what that status means, and any note attached to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      It reports what the dataset says and nothing beyond that. It cannot
      account for dose, timing, what else is in a body, or an individual
      medical picture — a pairing listed as lower risk is not a pairing
      cleared for you, and an unlisted pairing means the data is silent, not
      that there is nothing to know.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a medication is part of the picture, that is a question for a
      prescriber or pharmacist who can see your whole history. The
      <a href="/safety">safety page</a> has the routes.
    </p>
    <p class="detail">
      This page keeps nothing. Your choices are not saved, not sent anywhere,
      and are gone when you close the tab.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="tool">
    <CombinationLookup client:load />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  .tool {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .detail {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
